From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:24:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] meson: build the DRI frontend for softpipe on Darwin

EGL requires the DRI frontend, and a Darwin build enables that frontend
only for zink. A Darwin build whose only Gallium driver is softpipe, such
as one for a platform that has no Vulkan driver at all, therefore could not
enable EGL: configuration stopped with "EGL requires DRI, Haiku, Windows or
Android". Enable the frontend for softpipe on Darwin as well. The software
rasterizer then reaches EGL through the surfaceless platform's DRM-less
probe, exactly as zink does, and a build that includes zink is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index bda93d65d0d28cf6f06785b616949320f18ad4a8..9d7623b343ac9abed3dc529466e8942f0a2a9d79 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -362,7 +362,7 @@ with_vdrm = [
 ].contains(true)
 
 with_dri = false
-if with_gallium and (system_has_kms_drm or (with_gallium_zink and (freedreno_kmds.contains('kgsl') or host_machine.system() == 'darwin')))
+if with_gallium and (system_has_kms_drm or (with_gallium_zink and (freedreno_kmds.contains('kgsl') or host_machine.system() == 'darwin')) or (with_gallium_softpipe and host_machine.system() == 'darwin'))
   _glx = get_option('glx')
   _egl = get_option('egl')
   if _glx == 'dri' or _egl.enabled() or (_glx == 'disabled' and _egl.allowed())
